.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH tapectl-host-check 1  "tapectl-host-check " 
.SH NAME
tapectl\-host\-check \- Is this host quiet enough to write a tape?
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtapectl host check\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-unit\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Is this host quiet enough to write a tape?
.PP
Reports the load average, available memory, memory and I/O pressure, and any contender process or systemd unit (`[host_check]` in config.toml), the same check `volume write` runs before it touches the drive. Exit 0 when quiet, 1 when anything tripped. Never refuses anything: it only reports.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output in JSON format
.TP
\fB\-\-unit\fR \fI<UNIT>\fR
Also check this systemd unit (repeatable), on top of `[host_check] contender_units`, e.g. a CI runner\*(Aqs timer
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be done without making changes. Commands that cannot preview refuse the flag rather than ignore it (issue #241)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose output
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip ADR\-0008 Tier\-2 confirmation prompts. It never reaches a Tier\-3 refusal — those are facts, not risks to accept (issue #147)
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to config file.

NOTE: on its own this ALSO relocates the whole tapectl home to the config file\*(Aqs parent directory — database, keys, staging, receipts. That is how every test harness gets an isolated home, so it still works, but it is surprising enough that it now warns. Use \-\-home when you mean "operate on a different archive", and \-\-config only to point at a config file inside that home (issue #109).
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<HOME>\fR
tapectl home directory: database, keys, catalogs, receipts, logs.

Defaults to ~/.tapectl. The config file is taken from <home>/config.toml unless \-\-config overrides it. Also settable as TAPECTL_HOME (issue #109).
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
